---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="The Unleashing Flow methodology: Constraint → AI → Flow. A three-layer framework combining Theory of Constraints, flow-state design, and deep work principles."
>
  <section class="method-hero section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="section-label">The Methodology</p>
      <h1 class="method-title">Constraint → AI → Flow</h1>
      <p class="method-subtitle">
        Most businesses improve the wrong thing, build the fix wrong, and wonder why nobody uses it. This methodology addresses all three failures in sequence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Three Layers Overview -->
  <section class="layers-overview section">
    <p class="section-label">Three Layers</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Each layer builds on the one before it</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Skip a layer and the whole thing collapses: you automate the wrong thing, build a tool nobody can use, or watch freed capacity get swallowed by new shallow work.
    </p>

    <div class="layers-grid">
      <a href="#layer-1" class="layer-card">
        <span class="layer-number">Layer 1</span>
        <h3>Find the Constraint</h3>
        <p>Identify the ONE process that actually limits throughput right now. Don't guess. Don't automate what's convenient. Diagnose what's real.</p>
        <span class="layer-source">Theory of Constraints — Goldratt</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#layer-2" class="layer-card">
        <span class="layer-number">Layer 2</span>
        <h3>Build the Fix</h3>
        <p>Design the AI solution that targets the constraint — and build it so humans enter flow states instead of fighting the tool.</p>
        <span class="layer-source">Flow — Csikszentmihalyi · Deep Work — Newport · Hyperfocus — Bailey</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#layer-3" class="layer-card">
        <span class="layer-number">Layer 3</span>
        <h3>Sustain the Gain</h3>
        <p>Transform the work environment so freed capacity goes to deeper, more valuable work — not more shallow busywork.</p>
        <span class="layer-source">Organizational Flow · Deep Work Protocol</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- Layer 1 -->
  <section id="layer-1" class="layer-section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <span class="layer-badge">Layer 1</span>
      <h2 class="layer-title">Find the Constraint</h2>
      <p class="layer-intro">
        Every system has a constraint — the one point that limits its total throughput. Improving a non-constraint does not improve the system. It just creates excess capacity that piles up in front of the real bottleneck.
      </p>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h3>The Five Focusing Steps</h3>
        <div class="steps-list">
          <div class="focus-step">
            <span class="focus-label">Identify</span>
            <p>Where does work pile up? Where do customers wait? Where is the owner personally stuck in a repetitive loop?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="focus-step">
            <span class="focus-label">Exploit</span>
            <p>Squeeze every drop of capacity from the constraint without spending money. Remove waste, eliminate interruptions, ensure it never sits idle.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="focus-step">
            <span class="focus-label">Subordinate</span>
            <p>Everything else in the system serves the constraint. This means deliberately under-utilizing non-constraints — the hardest step because it offends the "keep everyone busy" instinct.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="focus-step">
            <span class="focus-label">Elevate</span>
            <p>If exploiting and subordinating aren't enough, invest to expand the constraint's capacity. This is where AI typically enters.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="focus-step">
            <span class="focus-label">Repeat</span>
            <p>The constraint has moved. Find the new one. This is a continuous cycle, not a one-time fix.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h3>Policy vs. Physical Constraints</h3>
        <p>The most impactful constraints are almost never physical. They're policy constraints — rules, habits, measurements, and procedures that nobody questions.</p>
        <blockquote>
          "Nobody knows the business like I do" is a policy constraint. "Every placement must go through the single coordinator" is a policy constraint. "We've always batched orders on Fridays" is a policy constraint.
        </blockquote>
        <p>AI aimed at a policy constraint that was never identified doesn't just fail — it makes a bad policy faster.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h3>The Effect-Cause-Effect Method</h3>
        <p>Finding constraints isn't about surveys or time studies. It's about logic:</p>
        <ol class="ece-list">
          <li>Start with an observable undesirable effect everyone agrees is real</li>
          <li>Hypothesize a cause — don't gather more data, think</li>
          <li>If that cause is real, predict a DIFFERENT effect that must also exist</li>
          <li>Check if the predicted effect exists</li>
          <li>Keep going deeper until you reach a cause that is psychological or procedural — that's the policy constraint</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Layer 2 -->
  <section id="layer-2" class="layer-section section">
    <span class="layer-badge dark">Layer 2</span>
    <h2 class="layer-title dark">Build the Fix — AI Designed for Flow</h2>
    <p class="layer-intro dark">
      The AI solution must be designed so the person using it can enter a flow state. Not just "work faster" — but work in a way that produces deep engagement, clear thinking, and sustained attention. This is the difference between a tool that gets adopted and one that gets abandoned.
    </p>

    <div class="flow-evidence">
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-stat">54%</span>
        <p>of work time spent in flow-like conditions when work is structured for it</p>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-stat">22 min</span>
        <p>recovery penalty every time a distraction breaks focused work</p>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-stat">40 bits/s</span>
        <p>conscious processing bandwidth — a single conversation uses most of it</p>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-stat">4 chunks</span>
        <p>working memory capacity — dashboards with 15 metrics are cognitively hostile</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-block">
      <h3>The Eight Conditions of Flow</h3>
      <p class="block-intro">Every AI solution is evaluated against Csikszentmihalyi's conditions. The tool should support as many as possible and violate none.</p>

      <div class="conditions-grid">
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Challenge-Skill Balance</h4>
          <p>The system dynamically adjusts human involvement. When a user is skilled, the AI handles more. When the situation is novel, the AI surfaces more information. The human always feels stretched but capable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Clear Goals</h4>
          <p>Every AI interface makes the current objective unmistakable. No ambiguous dashboards. The AI presents outputs in terms of the user's goal, not the system's internal logic.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Immediate Feedback</h4>
          <p>Real-time confirmation of progress. If the AI is processing, the human sees status evolving — not a loading screen. Batch processing is the enemy of flow. Stream results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Deep Concentration</h4>
          <p>The AI handles distracting peripheral tasks. The human does the thinking, deciding, and creating. The AI does NOT interrupt focused work with notifications or low-stakes approval requests.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Action-Awareness Merger</h4>
          <p>Minimize clicks, approvals, and context switches. The best AI tools feel like an extension of the person's thinking — not a separate system to manage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Sense of Control</h4>
          <p>The human always understands what the AI is doing and can override it. Transparency: here's what it decided, here's why, here's how to change it. Guardrails are visible and adjustable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Loss of Self-Consciousness</h4>
          <p>The tool never makes the user feel stupid. Error messages are constructive. The AI adapts to the user's level without making the adaptation visible or condescending.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="condition">
          <h4>Transformation of Time</h4>
          <p>Design for sustained engagement, not micro-interactions. Batch the AI's questions. Protect uninterrupted work blocks. Let the human set the pace.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-block">
      <h3>The Three Prongs of Implementation</h3>
      <p class="block-intro">Once the constraint is identified, the AI solution falls into one of three categories:</p>

      <div class="prongs-grid">
        <div class="prong">
          <span class="prong-number">1</span>
          <h4>Find More and Better Customers</h4>
          <p>AI for lead generation, qualification, personalized outreach, market analysis. Targets revenue-side constraints.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prong">
          <span class="prong-number">2</span>
          <h4>Automate and Improve Operations</h4>
          <p>AI for workflow automation, scheduling, inventory, fulfillment. Targets throughput constraints. The Goldratt test: is this aimed at THE bottleneck?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prong">
          <span class="prong-number">3</span>
          <h4>Make Humans Even Better</h4>
          <p>AI for decision support, knowledge management, training, quality control. Targets human-capacity constraints. This is where flow design matters most.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-block accent-block">
      <h3>The Acceleration Precept</h3>
      <p>Every AI solution is designed with a foundational reality: <strong>models are getting dramatically cheaper and smarter on a cycle measured in months.</strong></p>
      <div class="accel-grid">
        <div class="accel-item">
          <h4>Plan for Cheaper</h4>
          <p>Don't hardwire a specific model. Build abstraction layers. Design with model tiers — use the cheapest model that can handle each subtask. As costs drop, client economics improve automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="accel-item">
          <h4>Plan for Smarter</h4>
          <p>Architect solutions to absorb more capability as it becomes available. Identify the "waiting room" — tasks almost automatable today, six months from full automation. This turns one-time engagements into recurring relationships.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- Layer 3 -->
  <section id="layer-3" class="layer-section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <span class="layer-badge">Layer 3</span>
      <h2 class="layer-title">Sustain the Gain — Organizational Flow</h2>
      <p class="layer-intro">
        Without this layer, freed capacity fills with shallow work or the constraint moves and nobody notices. Layer 3 builds an organization where people do deep, valuable work by default.
      </p>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h3>Five Conditions of an Autotelic Work Environment</h3>
        <div class="auto-conditions">
          <div class="auto-condition">
            <h4>Clarity</h4>
            <p>Define outcomes, not activities. "Resolve 95% of customer issues within 24 hours" enables flow. "Answer the phone within three rings and follow the script" prevents it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="auto-condition">
            <h4>Centering</h4>
            <p>Value what people are doing in the present — their concrete work — rather than obsessing over future metrics and performance reviews.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="auto-condition">
            <h4>Choice</h4>
            <p>Provide the what and the why. Let people determine the how. The human should choose when and how to use the AI tool, not be forced into a rigid workflow.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="auto-condition">
            <h4>Commitment</h4>
            <p>Psychological safety. When AI systems make errors, blame the system design, not the human operator. Create an environment where people can hyperfocus without fear.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="auto-condition">
            <h4>Challenge</h4>
            <p>Every time a constraint is resolved and moves, the work changes. Roles evolve. Complexity increases naturally through the improvement cycle.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h3>The Deep Work Protocol</h3>
        <div class="protocol-grid">
          <div class="protocol-item">
            <span class="protocol-num">01</span>
            <h4>Ritualize Depth</h4>
            <p>Schedule blocks of uninterrupted deep work. No meetings, no Slack, no notifications. Start with 90-minute blocks and build the muscle.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="protocol-item">
            <span class="protocol-num">02</span>
            <h4>Batch the Shallow</h4>
            <p>Group email, admin tasks, and AI system oversight into defined periods. Build days around a core of deep work, shallow activities at the peripheries.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="protocol-item">
            <span class="protocol-num">03</span>
            <h4>Train the Attention Muscle</h4>
            <p>People who regularly practice concentration develop neural efficiency to enter flow more easily — their brains actually use LESS energy when focusing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="protocol-item">
            <span class="protocol-num">04</span>
            <h4>Embrace Productive Boredom</h4>
            <p>Intentional mind-wandering produces planning (48% of wandering time), creative connections, and self-awareness. Allow mental breathing room.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="protocol-item">
            <span class="protocol-num">05</span>
            <h4>Measure Depth, Not Activity</h4>
            <p>"How long would it take a smart recent grad to do this task?" If the answer is short, it's shallow work — and a candidate for AI automation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Convergence -->
  <section class="convergence section">
    <p class="section-label">The Cycle</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Where all three layers converge</h2>

    <div class="cycle-visual">
      <div class="cycle-step">
        <span class="cycle-num">1</span>
        <p><strong>Identify</strong> the current constraint</p>
      </div>
      <span class="cycle-arrow">&darr;</span>
      <div class="cycle-step">
        <span class="cycle-num">2</span>
        <p><strong>Exploit & subordinate</strong> — squeeze capacity without spending</p>
      </div>
      <span class="cycle-arrow">&darr;</span>
      <div class="cycle-step">
        <span class="cycle-num">3</span>
        <p><strong>Elevate</strong> with AI designed for flow</p>
      </div>
      <span class="cycle-arrow">&darr;</span>
      <div class="cycle-step">
        <span class="cycle-num">4</span>
        <p><strong>Absorb</strong> freed capacity into deep work</p>
      </div>
      <span class="cycle-arrow">&darr;</span>
      <div class="cycle-step">
        <span class="cycle-num">5</span>
        <p>Constraint has moved — <strong>repeat</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="convergence-note">
      Each round removes a constraint, adds intelligent automation, and deepens the quality of human work. Over time, the humans in the system are doing exclusively high-judgment, high-creativity work — while the AI handles everything that can be systematized.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Foundations -->
  <section class="foundations section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="section-label">The Intellectual Foundations</p>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="color: var(--ivory);">Built on decades of research</h2>

      <div class="foundations-grid">
        <div class="foundation-card">
          <h4>Goldratt</h4>
          <p class="foundation-work">Theory of Constraints</p>
          <p>The system has one constraint. Find it. Everything else is noise.</p>
          <span class="foundation-layer">Layer 1</span>
        </div>
        <div class="foundation-card">
          <h4>Csikszentmihalyi</h4>
          <p class="foundation-work">Flow</p>
          <p>Eight conditions of optimal experience. Work produces more flow than leisure when structured correctly.</p>
          <span class="foundation-layer">Layers 2 & 3</span>
        </div>
        <div class="foundation-card">
          <h4>Newport</h4>
          <p class="foundation-work">Deep Work</p>
          <p>Deep work is rare and valuable. Frenetic shallowness permanently damages focus capacity.</p>
          <span class="foundation-layer">Layers 2 & 3</span>
        </div>
        <div class="foundation-card">
          <h4>Bailey</h4>
          <p class="foundation-work">Hyperfocus</p>
          <p>40 bits/second. 4 chunks. Hyperfocus + scatterfocus as complementary modes of productive attention.</p>
          <span class="foundation-layer">Layer 2</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    heading="Ready to find your constraint?"
    subtext="The Throughput Diagnostic is where every engagement begins. We find the ONE thing limiting your business — then build the AI that fixes it."
  />
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .method-hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 100px 60px 80px;
  }

  .method-title {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--ivory);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .method-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--taupe);
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Layers Overview */
  .layers-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .layer-card {
    display: block;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #E8E0D6;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 32px 24px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 0.3s, transform 0.2s;
  }

  .layer-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--terracotta);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    color: inherit;
  }

  .layer-number {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--terracotta);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .layer-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .layer-card p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .layer-source {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: var(--taupe);
  }

  /* Layer Sections */
  .layer-section.section-dark {
    padding: 80px 60px;
  }

  .layer-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--terracotta-light);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    padding: 6px 16px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .layer-badge.dark {
    color: var(--terracotta);
    background: rgba(169,121,103,0.1);
  }

  .layer-title {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 36px);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ivory);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .layer-title.dark {
    color: var(--charcoal);
  }

  .layer-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--taupe);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .layer-intro.dark {
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }

  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .content-block h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .section-dark .content-block h3 {
    color: var(--ivory);
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .section-dark .content-block p {
    color: var(--taupe);
  }

  .block-intro {
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--terracotta-light);
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 20px 0;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--taupe);
  }

  /* Five Focusing Steps */
  .steps-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .focus-step {
    padding-left: 24px;
    border-left: 2px solid #4A3F3C;
  }

  .focus-label {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--terracotta-light);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  .focus-step p {
    color: var(--taupe);
  }

  .ece-list {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .ece-list li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--taupe);
  }

  /* Flow Evidence */
  .flow-evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .evidence-card {
    background: var(--charcoal);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 28px 20px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .evidence-stat {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--terracotta-light);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .evidence-card p {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--taupe);
  }

  /* Conditions Grid */
  .conditions-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .condition {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #E8E0D6;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 24px 20px;
  }

  .condition h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .condition p {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Prongs */
  .prongs-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .prong {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #E8E0D6;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 28px 24px;
  }

  .prong-number {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    background: var(--terracotta);
    color: var(--ivory);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .prong h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .prong p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Acceleration Precept */
  .accent-block {
    background: rgba(169,121,103,0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(169,121,103,0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 36px 32px;
  }

  .accel-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .accel-item h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .accel-item p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Layer 3 — Autotelic Conditions */
  .auto-conditions {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .auto-condition {
    padding-left: 24px;
    border-left: 2px solid #4A3F3C;
  }

  .auto-condition h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--terracotta-light);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .auto-condition p {
